---
title: "17 · The language model writes your lists"
lesson: "With a language model set in the gear (Krea 2's qwen3vl_4b, or a Qwen3-VL build), a library that does not exist yet is written the first time the node runs, using the lines around it as context. :20 tops a library up to at least 20 entries. New lists wait in the Libraries tab under To review until you Accept or Discard them. With an API endpoint, the 🎲 at the end of a line writes such a library before any run: steer it, pick the good entries and Keep as the library; Keep the direction keeps your steer with it for later top-ups."
tags: [tutorial, llm]
---
# Needs a language model: the gear → Model. Without one, unknown libraries are an error.
$shoe = __runway_shoes:20__
$venue = __unusual_runway_venue__
a runway photograph: a model walks through $venue in $shoe, direct on-camera flash, a crowded front row blurred at the edges
